--TEST--
A body key written at `Core\Http\Client::get` or `::head` is refused while compiling, because the verb is the member's own name — `rule:http-server/an-outbound-request-carries-one-body`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:http-server/an-outbound-request-carries-one-body`: a `GET` and a `HEAD` ask a question rather
// than carrying one, and octets attached to either are read by no server the
// request was worth making to. The verb is the member's own name and
// `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2 makes the bag a literal, so the refusal is made here rather
// than left to whatever the origin does with a body it did not expect.
string $url = "https://example.test/orders";

// The accepted half first: the same bag, minus the body — every other option
// is a question about how the request is made, and both verbs take all of them.
var $a = Core\Http\Client::get($url, {deadline: 5s, headers: ["accept" => "application/json"]});
var $b = Core\Http\Client::head($url, {followRedirects: 2});

// And the refusal, asked of each verb and of two different keys, so a check
// that learned one member's name or one key's would fail here.
var $c = Core\Http\Client::get($url, {json: ["id" => 7]});
var $d = Core\Http\Client::head($url, {body: "raw", contentType: "text/plain"});
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0816]: `Core\Http\Client::get` sends no body, and `json` is one
   --> case.nvs:16:39
%A
   = help: a `GET` asks a question rather than carrying one, and a server reads no body off it: put the value in the URL's query, or send it with the member whose verb takes a body
%A
error[E0816]: `Core\Http\Client::head` sends no body, and `body` is one
   --> case.nvs:17:40
%A
   = help: a `HEAD` asks a question rather than carrying one, and a server reads no body off it: put the value in the URL's query, or send it with the member whose verb takes a body
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
